{"name":"Greystone","hex":"#b7b9b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"greystone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of graystone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/greystone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Greystone Castle","blocks":[{"text":"Greystone Castle is a small Tudor style cottage in the Newlands Manor section of Reno, Nevada, USA. It was added to the National Register of Historic Places as an example of its architectural style as well as its ties into Reno's history as a migratory divorce town. Starting with the William E. Corey divorce, Reno became known for its much quicker and simpler divorce laws, the only requirement being that the individuals had to stay in town for six months to achieve residency. Greystone Castle is the type of smaller upscale housing that divorcing individuals used during their waiting period."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Greystone_Castle.jpg/330px-Greystone_Castle.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greystone_Castle","wikidata":"Q5608489"},{"title":"The Culinary Institute of America at Greystone","blocks":[{"text":"The Culinary Institute of America at Greystone is a branch campus of the private culinary college the Culinary Institute of America. The Greystone campus, located on State Route 29/128 in St. Helena, California, offers associate degrees and two certificate programs in culinary arts and baking and pastry arts. The CIA at Greystone and the Culinary Institute of America at Copia make up the school's California branch."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/USA-St._Helena-Greystone_Cellars-1.jpg/330px-USA-St._Helena-Greystone_Cellars-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Culinary_Institute_of_America_at_Greystone","wikidata":"Q5192950"},{"title":"Greystone (architecture)","blocks":[{"text":"Greystones are a style of residential building most commonly found in Chicago, Illinois, United States. As the name suggests, the buildings are typically grey in color and were most often built with Bedford Limestone quarried from South Central Indiana. In Chicago, there are roughly 30,000 greystones, usually built as a semi- or fully detached townhouse."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Dewes_House.JPG/330px-Dewes_House.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greystone_(architecture)","wikidata":"Q5608488"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Greystone_Cellars_1889.jpg/500px-Greystone_Cellars_1889.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Greystone_Cellars_1889.jpg/500px-Greystone_Cellars_1889.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Greystone Cellars in 1889","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreystone_Cellars_1889.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Greystone_Cellars_c1903_03.jpg/500px-Greystone_Cellars_c1903_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Greystone_Cellars_c1903_03.jpg/500px-Greystone_Cellars_c1903_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGreystone_Cellars_c1903_03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Greystone_Cellars_c1903_02.jpg/500px-Greystone_Cellars_c1903_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Greystone_Cellars_c1903_02.jpg/500px-Greystone